body:
`SentrySettings.dsn` is a required `str` with a built-in default, but docs suggest disabling Sentry via `PORTAL_SENTRY_DSN=""`. With the current type/absence of an “empty string → disabled” validator, setting an empty DSN will still be passed into `sentry_sdk.init(...)` and can raise at startup. Consider making `dsn` optional (e.g., `SecretStr | None`) and adding a validator that converts blank strings to `None`, then only initializing Sentry when a non-empty DSN is present.
```suggestion
    dsn: SecretStr | None = Field(
        default=SecretStr(
            "https://ee6ee87924219671e355dc1d4e237a67@o4508734372970496.ingest.us.sentry.io/4511135349080065"
        )
    )
    debug: bool = False

    @field_validator("dsn", mode="before")
    @classmethod
    def _empty_string_to_none(cls, v: str | SecretStr | None) -> str | SecretStr | None:
        if isinstance(v, str) and not v.strip():
            return None
        return v
```
